WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.664
This is Recetas, our family recipe collection.

00:00:03.138 --> 00:00:05.944
It starts with a scanned recipe, or even a
photo.

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:09.520
We keep the whole page, including handwritten
notes, then group

00:00:09.568 --> 00:00:12.979
the pages that belong together and leave out the
blank ones.

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.561
The import tools use OCR to read the scan.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.764
That gives us a starting point for the
ingredient list, with amounts

00:00:20.799 --> 00:00:21.565
and units.

00:00:22.308 --> 00:00:25.524
We check it against the original, especially
fractions and handwriting.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:30.180
These pomegranate bites span two pages, so we
keep both.

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.925
Now we can pick what we want to cook.

00:00:33.564 --> 00:00:37.593
For this shop, we're making chicken tacos and
pomegranate chocolate

00:00:37.616 --> 00:00:38.231
bites.

00:00:38.777 --> 00:00:43.734
Each recipe has its original pages and an
editable ingredient list.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:47.960
We add both recipes to the plan, and choose how
many batches to

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.051
make.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.122
Next, we check what we already have.

00:00:52.675 --> 00:00:56.063
Honey, cinnamon, olive oil and salt are in the
kitchen, so we don't

00:00:56.086 --> 00:00:57.109
need to buy them again.

00:00:57.862 --> 00:01:01.014
Recetas brings the recipe lists together and
combines matching

00:01:01.048 --> 00:01:01.637
amounts.

00:01:02.389 --> 00:01:05.988
We check the remaining pantry items and decide
how much to buy.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:10.548
Add to Family Cart uses our signed-in Chrome
browser.

00:01:11.187 --> 00:01:13.985
The helper searches Sprouts and checks the
family cart.

00:01:14.728 --> 00:01:16.887
It handles saved products automatically.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:21.810
For a new ingredient, we choose a product once,
and it remembers

00:01:21.857 --> 00:01:22.716
that choice.

00:01:23.354 --> 00:01:26.721
Weighed items, like this chicken, need a
quantity adjustment in

00:01:26.803 --> 00:01:27.557
Instacart.

00:01:28.416 --> 00:01:31.214
Then we continue with the rest of the list.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:34.459
Of course, the recipes aren't the whole shop.

00:01:35.097 --> 00:01:39.532
We also need bananas, strawberries and
blueberries, plus gluten-free

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:43.932
pie crusts, organic half-and-half and
unsweetened Ripple milk.

00:01:44.478 --> 00:01:47.102
These extras go into the same Sprouts family
cart.

00:01:47.566 --> 00:01:50.225
And because the helper checks what's already
there, it doesn't

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.779
add the same recipe products twice.

00:01:53.633 --> 00:01:58.579
At checkout, we review the delivery time, fees,
tip and total.

00:01:59.322 --> 00:02:03.954
Jordi's United Club card includes Instacart Plus
and two ten-dollar

00:02:04.012 --> 00:02:06.625
monthly credits, used on separate orders.

00:02:07.635 --> 00:02:12.023
Here, one credit takes ten dollars off, and
delivery is free.

00:02:12.661 --> 00:02:15.320
The service fee and tip still apply.

00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:19.407
The estimated total is ninety-eight dollars and
thirty cents.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.472
We check everything, then place the order.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.620
And there's the confirmation: a real family
order.

00:02:27.363 --> 00:02:29.778
The email arrives with the delivery window, too.

00:02:30.417 --> 00:02:34.829
We've gone from scanned recipes to a checked
ingredient list, skipped

00:02:34.852 --> 00:02:38.799
what's in the pantry, added a few household
extras, and placed

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:39.414
the order.

00:02:40.157 --> 00:02:44.290
Next time, the recipes and saved product choices
are ready to go.
